// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5955 new: Remote Debugging Detection for Linux and macOS (Chromium + Firefox)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5955
// Pull request author: Fz0x00
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Cookie Theft via Chromium Remote Debugging on Linux
// Sigma ID: 8263330b-3689-428b-b1ec-fe363579223a
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: PersonalRules
// Date: 2026-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1539
// Description: Detects the use of Chromium remote debugging arguments which can be abused to steal browser
//   cookies, session data, and credentials. An adversary may launch a browser with --remote-
//   debugging-port, --remote-debugging-pipe, or --remote-debugging-targets and connect via Chrome
//   DevTools Protocol to extract sensitive data without requiring any extension or exploit.
// False positives:
//   - Developers debugging browser extensions or web applications
//   - Automated testing frameworks using remote debugging
//   - CI/CD pipelines running browser automation tests
// References:
//   - https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/linux_debugging.md
//   - https://github.com/defaultnamehere/cookie_crimes
//   - https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/blob/master/documentation/modules/post/multi/gather/chrome_cookies.md
//   - https://posts.specterops.io/hands-in-the-cookie-jar-dumping-cookies-with-chromiums-remote-debugger-port-34c4f468844e
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/1170f436bbbf22972502a467ac84a05a81d07267/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_browsers_remote_debugging.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "--remote-debugging-port=" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--remote-debugging-pipe=" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--remote-debugging-targets=") and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "--remote-debugging-port=0"))
